Track 3: The Timing Board Misses One Second

Story & Context: An old mechanical timing board in the velodrome occasionally skips a second when its internal relay sticks. Marcus records the irregular click but refuses to quantize it. He inserts the missed-second pattern before selected drum restarts, turning the error into a structural hesitation inside an otherwise relentless 156 BPM track.

Lin holds one low bawu note across the hesitation and bends upward only when the kick returns. Zhao plays clipped metallic dyads on the expected beat, deliberately exposing the fact that the timing-board click is late. Eli sustains a soft euphonium pedal below both, creating a temporary low-frequency suspension.

Near the end, the timing-board sample disappears. The quartet keeps the same missing interval for three more cycles, proving that the fault has migrated from machine error into ensemble memory. The track ends on one unpitched bawu breath after the final kick mute.

